<odoo>
    <!-- Integrations Cycle 3 — the legacy ABM aggregations, as data.
         =============================================================
         Eight numbers the legacy application computed with inline arithmetic in
         `om_hr_payroll/models/hr_zoho_staging.py`, none of which existed
         anywhere a payroll officer could read them. They are rules now.

         THE NAMESPACE. `filter_expression` is evaluated by
         `hr.api.transformation.rule._execute_single` with exactly four names in
         scope: `rec` (the record's extracted_data dict), `env`, `datetime` and
         `date`. It is `rec`, NOT `record` — a filter written against `record`
         raises NameError, the engine's `except Exception: pass` swallows it,
         and the row is simply dropped from the aggregate. A whole feed would
         sum to zero with nothing in the log. Every expression below uses `rec`.

         THE DROPPED DATE FILTER. The legacy re-parsed each overtime record's
         `OT_Date` and re-checked it against the same window it had just asked
         the API for (:497-557). The endpoint is date-scoped by
         fromDate/toDate, so that second check could only ever remove records
         Zoho had already excluded — while silently dropping any record whose
         date string did not parse as dd-MM-yyyy. Dropped, deliberately; the
         window lives in the pull, which is the only place it can be enforced.

         PYTHON ROWS. Two of the eight are `python`, and neither is a shortcut:
         DEPCOUNT counts rows inside a TABULAR SECTION of one employee record,
         which no `count` over records can express, and WORKEDHRS has to add a
         seconds integer to an "H:MM" string. They ship as reviewed data and are
         not editable from any cockpit (W12) — the same rule the mapping canvas
         obeys for python transforms. Neither can raise: no expression below
         indexes, divides by a payload value, or calls anything that throws on
         an empty list, so an empty feed returns 0.0 by arithmetic rather than
         by the engine's default_value fallback. -->
    <data noupdate="1">

        <!-- ========== Zoho People — overtime bands ==========
             Legacy: hr_zoho_staging.py:497-557. One `sum_of_ot_hours_*`
             accumulator per band, all six reading `Actual_Pay_Hour` off the
             overtime_request form and all six requiring ApprovalStatus
             "Approved" — an unapproved request is a request, not an hour. -->

        <record id="trt_zoho_ot150" model="hr.api.transformation.rule.template">
            <field name="connector_type">zoho</field>
            <field name="output_key">OTHRS150</field>
            <field name="name">Overtime 150% — hours</field>
            <field name="rule_type">sum</field>
            <field name="source_data_type">custom</field>
            <field name="aggregate_field">Actual_Pay_Hour</field>
            <field name="filter_expression">rec.get('OT_Type') == '150%' and rec.get('ApprovalStatus') == 'Approved'</field>
            <field name="is_legacy_abm" eval="True"/>
            <field name="sequence">10</field>
            <field name="description">Approved overtime at the 150% band (normal weekday overtime
under Vietnamese labour law). Legacy: hr_zoho_staging.py:497-511.</field>
        </record>

